## 🎯 What's Working

### Real Image Loading ✅
- **Folder Selection Button** (top-right) - Click to select any image folder
- **AsyncImageProvider** - Loads real JPG, PNG, RAW (CR2, NEF, ARW, DNG), etc.
- **Viewport Culling** - Only loads visible thumbnails
- **Synthetic Test Data** - 10,000 colored rectangles on startup (for baseline testing)

### Performance Controls
- **Viewport Culling Toggle** - Enable/disable viewport-based loading
- **Frame Budget Slider** - 1-50 uploads per frame (default: 10)
- **Thumb Resolution Slider** - 128-512px (default: 256px ⭐)

### Real-Time Monitoring
- **FPS** - Color-coded (green ≥55, yellow ≥30, red <30)
- **Queue Depth** - Pending decode count
- **Memory Usage** - Live MB counter
- **Item Count** - Total items loaded

---

## 🧪 Testing Workflow

### 1. Baseline Test (Synthetic Data)
```
1. Launch appScrollBench.exe
2. Starts with 10,000 synthetic colored rectangles
3. Scroll rapidly - observe FPS and queue depth
4. Toggle optimizations on/off to see difference
```

### 2. Real Image Test
```
1. Click "📁 Select Folder" (top-right)
2. Choose a folder with 100+ images
3. Wait for scan to complete (watch console/logs)
4. Scroll through real images
5. Compare performance with different thumb resolutions
```

### 3. Performance Comparison
| Test | Viewport Culling | Frame Budget | Expected FPS | Expected Queue |
|------|-----------------|--------------|--------------|----------------|
| Baseline (off/off) | ❌ | ❌ | 10-20 | 200+ |
| Culling only | ✅ | ❌ | 30-40 | 50-100 |
| Budget only | ❌ | ✅ | 30-50 | 100+ |
| **Both (optimal)** | ✅ | ✅ | **50-60** | **<50** |

